{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'unresolved|change|why_changed|D728' DESIGN.md REQUEST-AUDIT.md gate.py ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -38; sed -n '11014,11060p' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10411:  review reopens at $0 (D542's five open items, the `reads`/`supports` separation, D538's seven filing changes), then goes to Alex\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10419:  round 2 DISAGREE with five changes, round 3 DISAGREE on one, all taken; consensus): for the product (poc-v118, no seed edges) a\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10449:  change is not opened (it returns after the July measurement, D693).\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10480:  product's own `model.call` cost records omit the cache-write premium too: a cost-reporting finding, recorded, not changed here.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10502:- **Open:** PRD 06 still says the default matcher is not asked for dependencies (true of poc-v118, the product); it changes with the\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10503:  decision that makes a linking version the product. The sourced-reference change (D693) waits for a longer linked run.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10552:  growth rate; no blanket ban on a whole reading its part). A wording change changes what the system does: it goes to Alex with the\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10569:- **The wording** (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md`, harness-only, no product file changed): a tie-break (when\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10594:## D706 · 2026-11-21 · poc-v120 (link questions version 2) passes council review as a product configuration; the paid design needs four changes\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10597:  unnamed there means `links-v1`, so poc-v119 is unchanged: checksum aa577d68c3148864); `links.READS_V2`, `SIGN_V2`, `QUESTION_SETS`\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10620:- **The council:** round 22 NOT READY (four changes), 23 (reading rule, freshness), 24 (three outcomes, product against infrastructure\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10681:  - The version: a judge version that changes the citation format only. Every id field (cites, push ids, `cites_views`, theme\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10687:- **Not done:** no paid call after the pilot, no product file changed.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10696:- **Scope:** a new judge version whose only change is the answer format's id fields (D711's recommendation). The link direction stays\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10717:  narrow its allowed set (a finding; frozen versions unchanged).\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10774:  - **Verdict:** format failure → confirmed failure (standing even when incomplete) → incomplete → unresolved → pass. Pass requires at\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10781:  Recorded as a finding; the frozen request is not changed.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10795:  A2 could change the verdict; unreadable answers and contradictory readings were counted; quotes were cut and multiline quotes lost;\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10866:- **The check that changed the frame:** the frozen judgement gold (D262).\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10878:  - **The judge flips:** linked-1 `8752`, `8756` and `8770` change what the same $387B basis includes, with no explanation.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10880:  - **Overlapping quarterly adjustments in old-3:** 4 clear (`4298`, `4510`, `5195`, `5369`) and 6 related. No rung change is\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10883:  - linked-1 made \"four unsupported increments, overlap unresolved\", not four proved double counts.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10886:  - The pilot's registered verdict (inconclusive) is unchanged.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10892:## D722 · 2026-11-22 · Alex closes the double-count design with nothing changed\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10896:  - 收尾，不改 (recommended: poc-v118 stays, the judge text unchanged, the findings recorded but not worked on, no spend);\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10916:  - the one-letter names in `judging._dependency_lines_full` are renamed (the rendered text is unchanged; the frozen pins pass);\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10928:  None is in the product path (poc-v118), and each fix would change pinned text or tested records, or redesign the linking version.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10950:    is unmeasured, and no change is made.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10951:  - A parallel replay left unfinished before 3ba40d8f cannot resume after it. The saved settings key changed with\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10953:- **3ba40d8f does not change poc-v118's judging or filing.** The v7 request matched byte for byte on 43 stored views. `maxItems` applies\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10983:  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10984:  - extraction unchanged;\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10989:- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11037:  Codex proposes leaving the earlier forecasts out of the calculation request and comparing after. That changes what the judge sees\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11039:- **Not done:** nothing sent; no product file changed; the paid gate not asked.\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11041:## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11051:  - whether a member's conclusion changed is derived by code afterwards, from its earlier rung, outcome and source figures;\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11053:- **D198 for judging-v7 is unchanged.**\n  - **Run 1 failed** on the gold's q19 (revenue over a per-unit price). The per-unit identity was added.\n  - **Runs 2 to 6** pass the registered items, the fixtures growing from 29 to 41 as each council round added variants.\n  - **The mutants:** 15 of 15 are caught, and the unmutated control passes.\n  - **The rendered request:** one stored family (old-2 at 09-20) is rendered: system text 4,835 characters (v7 4,924), user message\n    123,304 characters, 237 evidence items. A conforming answer passes the schema and the checks.\n- **What it established:**\n  - each of the five stored defects is caught by its named check:\n    - a segment quarter above the company quarter;\n    - two Q3 bases;\n    - an unknown-overlap addition shown with its $35B alternate;\n    - a scope conversion with no stated assumption;\n    - a trim across $40B;\n  - the self-made $414B reference is refused;\n  - the four gold reasonings (q01, q02, q19, q22) are expressible.\n- **Council rounds 46f to 46j, each GATE FAIL:** every round found a variant by which a model could relabel or route around a\n  structural check. The two recurring mechanisms were answered with one structural rule each in v9:\n  - scenario membership derived along the whole path;\n  - earlier-forecast status derived from the basis or a pointer.\n- **Open after round 46j** (`codex-r46j.md`):\n  1. scenario names can still separate a part from its whole; related outcomes must cover the same scenarios;\n  2. the range rule refuses q22's reuse of q01's range; C9 must work per scenario;\n  3. an earlier forecast restated as a fresh estimate is invisible to code.\n\n  Codex proposes leaving the earlier forecasts out of the calculation request and comparing after. That changes what the judge sees\n  (D198: the previous conclusion carries the pieces not shown), so it goes to Alex.\n- **Not done:** nothing sent; no product file changed; the paid gate not asked.\n\n## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n\n- **The question** (after D727): \"新判官算数的时候，要不要让它看到自己上一次的预测？… 不给看的代价：以前靠'上次结论'带着的那些老证据（这次没展示的）就丢了，只剩最近被引用过的和新到的证据。\"\n  Options:\n  - 算的时候不给看 (recommended: compute from the evidence alone, then compare with the earlier conclusion; the old pieces' carried\n    effect is lost and is measured in the paid test);\n  - 照旧给看.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"算的时候不给看 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex), for judging-v13:**\n  - the calculation request shows no earlier forecast;\n  - whether a member's conclusion changed is derived by code afterwards, from its earlier rung, outcome and source figures;\n  - the evidence in view stays D198's arrivals and basis.\n- **D198 for judging-v7 is unchanged.**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
