{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'unresolved|changed' DESIGN.md gate.py | tail -28; sed -n '10963,10993p' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"DESIGN.md:22:| Previous conclusion | rung and reasons, cut at 800 characters, unmarked | **not shown** (D728). Whether a member's conclusion changed is derived by code afterwards from its earlier rung, outcome and source figures (`calc_check.changed`) |\nDESIGN.md:25:| Failure | refused twice: the question is left as it was | refused twice: the family is recorded **unresolved** and no member is updated. A member may also answer `unresolved` itself (§2) [46.5] |\nDESIGN.md:48:             reasons, cites, pushes, theme_pushes, changed, why_changed }\nDESIGN.md:49:         | { view_id, shape: \"unresolved\", why, cites, changed, why_changed } ]       # no outcome, no rung\nDESIGN.md:96:  boundary-deciding assumption is supported. D721/D722: unresolved inclusion is never treated as proof of double counting.\nDESIGN.md:106:- **`unresolved`:** read by the round (no member updated) and the bundle (\"Forecast unavailable\", D726).\nDESIGN.md:114:- v7's request bytes are unchanged (the frozen pins).\nDESIGN.md:123:| second refusal | the family is unresolved, recorded |\nDESIGN.md:124:| a member's own `unresolved` [46b.5] | recorded; the family is held (no member updated) when any other member's outcome depends on a shared quantity or relation involving it; otherwise the others publish if they pass |\nDESIGN.md:136:- D711, D721, D722: linking passed conclusions, and unresolved inclusion is not double counting.\nDESIGN.md:148:- **Added:** how to write figures (kinds, bases, expressions, relations, bridges, `adjusts`, `unresolved`).\nDESIGN.md:149:- **The audit:** every changed sentence is shown with its source (D260, D263, D725, this design), read against a stored family\nDESIGN.md:165:| U1–U2 (paths) | a member answering `unresolved` while another member's outcome needs its shared quantity; a calculation refused twice | the family held, recorded; the family unresolved, recorded |\ngate.py:58:            'pushes': [], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': 'w'}\ngate.py:350:                            'basis_text': 'unchanged', 'rests_on': [], 'value': 1.0})\ngate.py:402:    ch1 = cc.changed(dict(prev, outcome=418.4), calc_c['answers'][0], figs_c)\ngate.py:403:    ch2 = cc.changed(dict(prev, rung=3, outcome=387.0), calc_c['answers'][0], figs_c)\ngate.py:404:    sib = copy.deepcopy(calc_c)                       # [46k.3] a sibling-only source change leaves v14 unchanged\ngate.py:408:    ch3 = cc.changed(dict(prev, outcome=418.4), sib['answers'][0], dict(sib_figs, mix=dict(sib_figs['mix'], expression='92.5% (restated)')))\ngate.py:414:    ch5 = cc.changed({'rung': 3, 'outcome': 52.70, 'sources': own5}, c5['answers'][0], f5)\ngate.py:424:    ch6 = cc.changed({'rung': 3, 'outcome': [None, 39.0, '<'], 'sources': own6}, c6['answers'][0], f6)\ngate.py:425:    ch6b = cc.changed({'rung': 3, 'outcome': r6['published']['v41'], 'sources': own6}, c6['answers'][0], f6)\ngate.py:427:    rows.append(('CH1', ch1[0] is False, f'unchanged: {ch1[1]}', {'errors': [], 'recorded': []}))\ngate.py:428:    rows.append(('CH2', ch2[0] is True and 'rung 3 to 2' in ch2[1], f'changed: {ch2[1]}', {'errors': [], 'recorded': []}))\ngate.py:433:    ch4 = cc.changed({'rung': 2, 'outcome': (390.0, 445.0), 'sources': own_g}, c1g['answers'][0], figs_g)\ngate.py:662:    u1['answers'][1] = {'view_id': 'v9', 'shape': 'unresolved', 'why': 'the segment mix after Q2 is not stated', 'cites': [], 'changed': True,\ngate.py:663:                        'why_changed': 'w'}\ngate.py:669:    rows.append(('U2', outcome == 'unresolved', f'two refusals give {outcome}', res_bad))\n  - Claude's reflection was written before Codex's.\n  - Codex ran an independent investigation (fresh thread `01a20501…`) and a challenge round.\n  - Consensus. One wording point stays open: the $146B is arithmetically a residual, but the order of the judge's choices is unknown.\n- **Diagnosis:**\n  1. Answers are prose; code ties no figure to a source and recomputes nothing. The production check passes contradictory or invented\n     figures.\n  2. Related questions compute the same quantities separately. The unit is one question, with 0 dependencies.\n  3. Filing and the evidence in view split their inputs. The previous conclusion carries figures without provenance.\n  4. Opening's bands amplify an error.\n- **Measured:**\n  - Data Center Q4 above company Q4 on at least 13 of 26 days in old-1;\n  - Data Center's full year above the total's on 20 consecutive days in old-2;\n  - different Q3 bases on 17 of 18 paired days;\n  - shared evidence between total and Data Center 8% in old-2;\n  - 17 of the 24 double-rejected answers from unchecked arithmetic.\n- **Recommended design** (a new judge version, Alex's to open):\n  - one judging call per related family, each question keeping its answer from one calculation;\n  - figures labelled by the judge (source, calculation, assumption; scope and period);\n  - code checks only identity and arithmetic (figure in quote, recompute, part within whole, one value per shared quantity, a sourced\n    reference);\n  - unreconciled forecasts shown as unresolved;\n  - extraction unchanged;\n  - families declared for the test.\n- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\n- **The test:** a $0 gate (hand reconstructions of five stored cases, four gold controls, three planted errors), then a paid gate\n  (36 calls; joint against separate on the three draws' 09-20 pair, plus O, S and E singletons). Pass and stop lines are in `RESULT.md`.\n- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n\n## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n\n- **The questions** (after D725):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '72,103p' calc_check.py; sed -n '104,126p' DESIGN.md; sed -n '11041,11054p' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '60,78p' render_v13.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '72,103p' calc_check.py; sed -n '104,126p' DESIGN.md; sed -n '11041,11054p' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '60,78p' render_v13.py\"","aggregated_output":"\n\ndef _same(a, b):\n    return a is not None and b is not None and abs(a - b) <= 1e-9 * max(1.0, abs(b))\n\n\ndef _source_errors(fig, passages):\n    passage = passages.get(fig.get('evidence'))\n    if passage is None:\n        return [('C1', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: evidence {fig.get(\"evidence\")} was not shown')]\n    matches = [e for e in extract(passage['text']) if e['text'] == fig.get('expression')]\n    if not matches:\n        return [('C1', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: \"{fig.get(\"expression\")}\" is not a complete numeric expression of {fig[\"evidence\"]}')]\n    expr, comp = matches[0], fig.get('component', 'value')\n    bound, unit = fig.get('bound'), fig.get('unit')\n    ok = False\n    if comp == 'value' and expr['form'] in ('money', 'money_plain', 'percent'):\n        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr['value']) and unit == expr['unit'] and bound == expr.get('bound')\n    elif comp == 'bound' and expr['form'] in ('qualified', 'percent'):\n        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr['value']) and unit == expr['unit'] and bound == expr['bound'] and bound is not None\n    elif comp == 'midpoint' and expr['form'] == 'relative':\n        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr['midpoint']) and unit == 'USD bn' and bound is None\n    elif comp == 'relative' and expr['form'] == 'relative':\n        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr['relative']) and unit == '%' and bound is None\n    elif comp in ('low', 'high') and expr['form'] == 'range':\n        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr[comp]) and unit == 'USD bn' and bound is None\n    elif comp == 'multiplier' and expr['form'] == 'multiplier':\n        ok = _same(fig.get('value'), expr['multiplier']) and unit == 'x' and bound == expr['bound']\n    if not ok:\n        return [('C1', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: value {fig.get(\"value\")} {unit} bound {bound} does not equal \"{expr[\"text\"]}\" as component {comp}')]\n    return []\n\n- **The calculation, the recorded assumptions and band-deciding flags:** read by the checks, the readers' packets, and later the\n  page.\n- **`unresolved`:** read by the round (no member updated) and the bundle (\"Forecast unavailable\", D726).\n- **The family declaration:** read by the request builder, C3, C4 and C7.\n- **Nothing in poc-v118 reads any of it.**\n\n**New path × old checks.**\n- v7's id, push and theme checks apply per member answer. Rung checks apply to `forecast` answers only [46b.5]. `cites` names shown\n  evidence only.\n- `cites_views` is always empty.\n- v7's request bytes are unchanged (the frozen pins).\n\n**State × event (the test harness).** Inputs are fixed: the stored requests' passages and the gold packet's items, as of the stored\nday.\n\n| Event | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| success | the calculation and answers are recorded with their check results |\n| refusal | the errors are recorded; one retry with them |\n| second refusal | the family is unresolved, recorded |\n| a member's own `unresolved` [46b.5] | recorded; the family is held (no member updated) when any other member's outcome depends on a shared quantity or relation involving it; otherwise the others publish if they pass |\n| crash midway | the attempt is recorded incomplete and counts as no result |\n\n## D728 · 2026-11-22 · Alex: the family judge does not see its earlier forecasts while calculating\n\n- **The question** (after D727): \"新判官算数的时候，要不要让它看到自己上一次的预测？… 不给看的代价：以前靠'上次结论'带着的那些老证据（这次没展示的）就丢了，只剩最近被引用过的和新到的证据。\"\n  Options:\n  - 算的时候不给看 (recommended: compute from the evidence alone, then compare with the earlier conclusion; the old pieces' carried\n    effect is lost and is measured in the paid test);\n  - 照旧给看.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"算的时候不给看 (推荐)\".\n- **Decided (Alex), for judging-v13:**\n  - the calculation request shows no earlier forecast;\n  - whether a member's conclusion changed is derived by code afterwards, from its earlier rung, outcome and source figures;\n  - the evidence in view stays D198's arrivals and basis.\n- **D198 for judging-v7 is unchanged.**\n    })\n    push = obj({'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    theme_push = obj({'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': theme_ids or ['none']},\n                      'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    answer = obj({\n        'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids},\n        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\n        'outcome': nullable(S), 'rung': nullable({'type': 'integer'}),\n        'reference': nullable(obj({'figure': nullable(S), 'unavailable': nullable(S)}, 'An external figure, or a calculation from external '\n                              'and reported figures, or unavailable with why.')),\n        'reasons': S, 'why': nullable(S),\n        'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}},\n        'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': push}, 'theme_pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': theme_push},\n    })\n    return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure}, 'answers': {'type': 'array', 'items': answer}})\n\n\ndef parts(user):\n    head, rest = user.split('\\n\\n[Evidence in view', 1)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport pathlib,json,io,contextlib,types\nimport gate, calc_check, render_v13, mutants\ndef replay(func, log):\n    p=io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(p): status=func()\n    assert status==0 and p.getvalue()==pathlib.Path(log).read_text()\nreplay(gate.main,'\\\\''gate-run25.txt'\\\\'')\nassert gate.MANIFEST==json.loads(pathlib.Path('\\\\''gate-run25.fixtures.json'\\\\'').read_text())\nreplay(render_v13.main,'\\\\''render-r1.txt'\\\\'')\noriginal=gate.cc\npath=pathlib.Path('\\\\''calc_check.py'\\\\'')\nsrc=path.read_text()\nfor name,old,new,target in mutants.MUTANTS:\n    gate.cc=original\n    if old:\n        assert src.count(old)==1,name\n        mod=types.ModuleType('\\\\''in_memory_calc_check'\\\\'')\n        exec(compile(src.replace(old,new),str(path),'\\\\''exec'\\\\''),mod.__dict__)\n        gate.cc=mod\n    misses={name for name,ok,_,_ in gate.run() if not ok}\n    assert (target in misses if target else not misses),(name,misses)\nprint('\\\\''85 gate items, 45 mutants and stored render reproduced'\\\\'')\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
